      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let's find the decimal representation of 1/7. When we divide 1 by 7, we get:\n\n1 ÷ 7 = 0.142857142857...\n\nThe decimal representation of 1/7 is a repeating decimal with the digits \"142857\" repeating indefinitely. The length of the repeating sequence is 6.\n\nTo find the 100th digit after the decimal point, we need to determine the position of the 100th digit within the repeating sequence. We can do this by finding the remainder when 100 is divided by the length of the repeating sequence (6).\n\n100 ÷ 6 = 16 remainder 4\n\nThis tells us that the 100th digit corresponds to the 4th digit in the repeating sequence \"142857\". The 4th digit is 5.\n\nTherefore, the 100th digit after the decimal point of the decimal representation of 1/7 is \\(\\boxed{5}\\).",
